    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11134" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏralli</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Lower Mœsia, on the Danube, on the coast
				of the Black Sea</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 4, 2, 37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 8,
			83</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrallĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				<i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				the Coralli</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pelagus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 6</span></i>
			.</div>
